{"id": "EUVD-2026-103314", "enisaUuid": "c65c9f07-d21d-3e0f-a6bf-4f233c7eaeb8", "description": "phpMyFAQ before 4.1.9 and 4.2.0-alpha before 4.2.0-beta contains a cross-site request forgery vulnerability in the Elasticsearch and OpenSearch administration API endpoints, which do not validate a CSRF token for the create, drop, and import actions. Attackers can lure a user with CONFIGURATION_EDIT permission to a malicious page that triggers these actions, deleting search indexes, forcing re-indexing, or exhausting resources.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T14:52:20", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-cmvh-fpmf-8gfx", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-before-4.1.9-and-4.2.0-alpha-before-4.2.0-beta-csrf-in-elasticsearch-opensearch-admin-api-index-operations"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111906", "GHSA-4qjm-33q6-wmgj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "97084500-3423-3301-ab53-2521fb779422", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.1.9"}, {"id": "c7ff9313-43c2-3d99-bcd0-1e751ee100c0", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0-alpha <4.2.0-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4bb92195-e1dd-31ff-8fb9-d33e0aea7834", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}